{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>But torn, etc.</b> In saying <b>but</b> he alluded that he was only minimally torn, for he is neither in the distress of servitude nor in the distress of imprisonment. Therefore he concluded <b>and I have not seen him until now</b> — this indicates that he exists in being, only he has not seen him until now." "<b>Further,</b> it intends in saying <b>but torn</b> etc., meaning, ״but״ — a diminishment, specifically regarding the tearing. But regarding what he said (Genesis 37:33) ״חַיָּה רָעָה אֲכָלָתְהוּ״, concerning which they of blessed memory said (Genesis Rabbah 84) that the allusion was to the wife of Potiphar — in this there is no diminishment, for through our sins it was what it was, which caused him to lose ten sons that he was destined to father [so as] to establish twelve tribes, as they of blessed memory said (Sotah 36b), and through the intermediary of the wicked woman ten drops fell from him, and only two emerged from him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:41.760879537Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}